meta {
  name: Login
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "device_id": "{{device_id}}",
    "device_token": "{{device_token}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const body = res.getBody();
  if (body && body.access_token) {
    bru.setEnvVar("jwt_token", body.access_token);
    bru.setEnvVar("refresh_token", body.refresh_token);
  }
}

docs {
  Exchange device credentials for a JWT access+refresh pair.

  Request:
    device_id     — UUID from /auth/pair/complete
    device_token  — 64-hex token from /auth/pair/complete

  Success (200):
    {
      "access_token":  "<jwt>",   // HS256, ~1h TTL
      "refresh_token": "<jwt>",   // HS256, ~30d TTL
      "expires_in":    3600        // access TTL in seconds
    }
  Both jti's are written into the `sessions` table. Auth middleware checks
  every protected request against that table — revocation works in real time.

  Failures:
    401 DEVICE_NOT_FOUND  → device_id unknown
    401 DEVICE_INACTIVE   → device exists but disabled
    401 INVALID_TOKEN     → device_token mismatch (Argon2 verify)
    429                   → rate limit (5 burst, ~1/12s replenish per IP)

  The access token is auto-saved as `jwt_token` and used by all bearer-auth
  requests in this collection.
}
